Current Terraform file ({{ $('JS - Identify Root-Cause Commit').item.json.terraformPath }}), base64-encoded content:
{{ $json.content }}

Decode the base64 content mentally, review it for likely cost drivers tied to the top contributing service (oversized instance types, high desired_count/min/max, over-provisioned storage or throughput, missing lifecycle rules, orphaned NAT gateways, etc.), and:
1. Write a rootCauseSummary (2-3 sentences) explaining the likely cause.
2. Write a suggestedFixDescription (2-4 sentences) explaining the proposed change.
3. Produce updatedFileContent: the COMPLETE corrected file content (plain text, not base64) with a conservative, safe fix applied — keep all unrelated content unchanged.
4. prBranchName: a short kebab-case branch name.
5. prTitle: a concise PR title.
6. prBody: a markdown PR description including the root cause, the fix, and the cost impact figures above.
7. commitMessage: a concise commit message.

Return ONLY a JSON object with keys: rootCauseSummary, suggestedFixDescription, updatedFileContent, prBranchName, prTitle, prBody, commitMessage. No markdown fences, no commentary.

